      "message": "Should this #if macro just be checking _WIN32? In my opinion, platform-specific ifdefs are easier to reason about, because you do not have to do any additional research about which platform supports F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC.\n\n#if !defined(_WIN32) // Windows does not have F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC\n    unique_fd dup_fd(::fcntl(fd, F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC, 0));\n#else \n    unique_fd dup_fd(::dup(fd));\n#endif",
